---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="physics"
  title="Entropy"
  description="A macrostate is what you can see: how many particles are on the left. A microstate is the full detail: which ones. Entropy just counts how many microstates wear the same macrostate, S = k ln Ω, and that counting alone is enough to make time run one way."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="ent" width="900" height="630"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="step">Step</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">All left</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Particles N <b id="nval">40</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="4" max="200" step="2" value="40" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Speed <b id="spval">30/s</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="sp" min="0" max="100" value="45" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>1 step / 2 s</span><span>5000 / s</span></div>
      </div>

      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="hist" checked /> Overlay measured visit frequency</label>

      <div>
        <div class="micro-label" id="microcap">Other arrangements that look the same from outside</div>
        <canvas id="micro" class="mini-canvas" width="300" height="132"></canvas>
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span>What you see</span><b id="nl">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Ways to arrange it Ω</span><b id="omega">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Entropy S/k = ln Ω</span><b id="ent-s">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Largest possible S/k</span><b id="smax">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Share of all arrangements</span><b id="share">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Steps taken</span><b id="steps">0</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Back to all-left after</span><b id="recur">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>…at the current speed</span><b id="recur-t">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        One step moves a single randomly chosen particle to the other side. The
        rule has no preferred direction, and no particle knows where it should
        be. Everything you see comes from counting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Slow the speed right down to a step every second or two and watch single
      moves. Each one is a coin flip with no bias at all, yet the pile on the
      left keeps shrinking. Nothing pushes the particles right; there are just
      far more ways to be mixed than to be sorted.
    </li>
    <li>
      Compare the two rows above the chart. The <b>microstate</b> strip changes
      at every single step. The <b>macrostate</b> beside it, just a count, barely
      moves. Entropy is the size of the gap: how many different strips give the
      same count.
    </li>
    <li>
      Look at the two curves in the chart. The bars are the <b>entropy</b>
      S(n) = ln Ω(n), a broad gentle hill. The line is the <b>probability</b>
      Ω(n)/2<sup>N</sup>, a razor-thin spike. Probability is the exponential of
      entropy, so a mild bump in S becomes an overwhelming bias in P. That single
      fact is the second law.
    </li>
    <li>
      Drop N to <b>4 or 6</b>. Entropy now visibly falls as often as it rises,
      and the system returns to all-left every so often. The second law is not a
      prohibition, it is a statement about odds, and the odds are only unbeatable
      when N is large.
    </li>
    <li>
      Raise N back to <b>200</b> and read the recurrence time. Nothing forbids
      every particle from crowding left again, it simply takes longer than the
      universe has existed. Irreversibility is about counting, not about the laws
      of motion.
    </li>
    <li>
      With the overlay on, the measured <b>visit frequency</b> settles onto the
      Ω(n)/2<sup>N</sup> curve. Time spent in a macrostate is proportional to how
      many microstates it owns: entropy is a census, and the dynamics just takes
      it.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas } from '../../../lib/sim';
  import { equationBar } from '../../../lib/equation';

  // --- combinatorics -------------------------------------------------------
  // Ω(n) = C(N, n) runs past 10^59 for N = 200, so everything is done in logs.
  function lgamma(x: number): number {
    const g = 7;
    const c = [
      0.99999999999980993, 676.5203681218851, -1259.1392167224028,
      771.32342877765313, -176.61502916214059, 12.507343278686905,
      -0.13857109526572012, 9.9843695780195716e-6, 1.5056327351493116e-7,
    ];
    if (x < 0.5) return Math.log(Math.PI / Math.sin(Math.PI * x)) - lgamma(1 - x);
    x -= 1;
    let a = c[0];
    const t = x + g + 0.5;
    for (let i = 1; i < g + 2; i++) a += c[i] / (x + i);
    return 0.5 * Math.log(2 * Math.PI) + (x + 0.5) * Math.log(t) - t + Math.log(a);
  }
  const lnChoose = (N: number, n: number) =>
    lgamma(N + 1) - lgamma(n + 1) - lgamma(N - n + 1);

  /** Render a count given only its natural log: exact when small, else 1.2×10^34. */
  /** Ω as TeX: a plain integer while it is small, then a proper power of ten. */
  function texBig(ln: number) {
    if (ln < 13) return String(Math.round(Math.exp(ln)));
    const e = ln / Math.LN10;
    const p = Math.floor(e);
    return `${Math.pow(10, e - p).toFixed(2)}\\times 10^{${p}}`;
  }

  function fromLn(ln: number) {
    if (ln < 13) return String(Math.round(Math.exp(ln)));
    const e = ln / Math.LN10;
    const p = Math.floor(e);
    const m = Math.pow(10, e - p);
    return `${m.toFixed(2)}×10^${p}`;
  }

  // Slider 0..100 maps to steps per second across four decades, so the left
  // end is slow enough to follow one particle at a time.
  const stepsPerSecond = (v: number) => 0.5 * Math.pow(10, v / 25);

  // --- state ---------------------------------------------------------------
  const state = { N: 40, speed: 45, running: true, hist: true };
  let side: Uint8Array; // 0 = left, 1 = right, per particle
  let xL: Float64Array, xR: Float64Array, yPos: Float64Array; // resting spots
  let anim: Float64Array; // 0..1 slide progress after a jump
  let visits: Float64Array; // how often each macrostate was seen
  let lnOmega: Float64Array;
  let trace: number[] = [];
  let steps = 0;
  let nLeft = 0;
  let lastMoved = -1;
  let lastMovedAge = 99;

  function build() {
    const N = state.N;
    side = new Uint8Array(N);
    xL = new Float64Array(N);
    xR = new Float64Array(N);
    yPos = new Float64Array(N);
    anim = new Float64Array(N);
    visits = new Float64Array(N + 1);
    lnOmega = new Float64Array(N + 1);
    for (let n = 0; n <= N; n++) lnOmega[n] = lnChoose(N, n);
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      xL[i] = 0.05 + 0.4 * Math.random();
      xR[i] = 0.55 + 0.4 * Math.random();
      yPos[i] = 0.06 + 0.88 * Math.random();
      anim[i] = 1;
    }
    reset();
  }
  function reset() {
    side.fill(0);
    anim.fill(1);
    visits.fill(0);
    trace = [];
    steps = 0;
    nLeft = state.N;
    lastMoved = -1;
    lastMovedAge = 99;
    visits[nLeft] = 1;
  }

  /** One Ehrenfest step: pick a particle at random, send it to the other side. */
  function stepOnce() {
    const i = (Math.random() * state.N) | 0;
    side[i] = side[i] ? 0 : 1;
    nLeft += side[i] ? -1 : 1;
    anim[i] = 0;
    lastMoved = i;
    lastMovedAge = 0;
    steps++;
    visits[nLeft]++;
  }

  // --- canvas --------------------------------------------------------------
  const canvas = document.getElementById('ent') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const css = (v: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(v).trim();
  const ink = () => css('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const ACC = '#7c8cff', WARM = '#f59e0b';

  const BOX = { x: 24, y: 34, w: W - 48, h: 190 };
  const STRIP = { x: 24, y: 262, w: W - 48, h: 22 };
  const CH = { x: 62, y: 348, w: W - 100, h: 132 };
  const TR = { x: 62, y: 530, w: W - 100, h: 78 };

  function label(text: string, x: number, y: number, alpha = 0.55, align: CanvasTextAlign = 'left', size = 12) {
    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${ink()},${alpha})`;
    ctx.font = `${size}px ui-monospace, monospace`;
    ctx.textAlign = align;
    ctx.fillText(text, x, y);
    ctx.textAlign = 'left';
  }

  function drawBox() {
    const N = state.N;
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.25)`;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.strokeRect(BOX.x, BOX.y, BOX.w, BOX.h);

    const mid = BOX.x + BOX.w / 2;
    ctx.setLineDash([6, 5]);
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.3)`;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(mid, BOX.y);
    ctx.lineTo(mid, BOX.y + BOX.h);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    const r = Math.max(3, Math.min(9, 260 / Math.sqrt(N * 40)));
    const showIds = N <= 12;
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      const home = side[i] ? xR[i] : xL[i];
      const from = side[i] ? xL[i] : xR[i];
      const t = anim[i];
      const e = t * t * (3 - 2 * t); // smoothstep the slide across the divider
      const fx = from + (home - from) * e;
      const px = BOX.x + fx * BOX.w;
      const py = BOX.y + yPos[i] * BOX.h;
      // halo on the particle that just moved, so a single step is followable
      if (i === lastMoved && lastMovedAge < 1) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},${0.75 * (1 - lastMovedAge)})`;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(px, py, r + 5 + 6 * lastMovedAge, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.stroke();
      }
      ctx.fillStyle = side[i] ? WARM : ACC;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.9;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(px, py, r, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      if (showIds) {
        ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,11,14,0.85)';
        ctx.font = '10px ui-monospace, monospace';
        ctx.textAlign = 'center';
        ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
        ctx.fillText(String(i + 1), px, py + 0.5);
        ctx.textBaseline = 'alphabetic';
        ctx.textAlign = 'left';
      }
    }

    ctx.font = '600 13px ui-monospace, monospace';
    ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
    ctx.fillText(`LEFT  ${nLeft}`, BOX.x + 10, BOX.y - 12);
    ctx.textAlign = 'right';
    ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
    ctx.fillText(`${N - nLeft}  RIGHT`, BOX.x + BOX.w - 10, BOX.y - 12);
    ctx.textAlign = 'left';

    // narration of the move, readable only when the pace is slow
    if (lastMoved >= 0 && lastMovedAge < 1 && stepsPerSecond(state.speed) < 12) {
      const dir = side[lastMoved] ? 'left → right' : 'right → left';
      label(`particle ${lastMoved + 1}:  ${dir}`, BOX.x + BOX.w / 2, BOX.y + BOX.h + 18, 0.5 * (1 - lastMovedAge), 'center');
    }
  }

  /** The full detail (which particle is where) next to the count it collapses to. */
  function drawStrip() {
    const N = state.N;
    label('MICROSTATE: which particle is where, one cell each', STRIP.x, STRIP.y - 10, 0.45);
    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.8)`;
    ctx.font = '600 12px ui-monospace, monospace';
    ctx.textAlign = 'right';
    ctx.fillText(`MACROSTATE: ${nLeft} left, ${N - nLeft} right`, STRIP.x + STRIP.w, STRIP.y - 10);
    ctx.textAlign = 'left';

    const cw = STRIP.w / N;
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      const x = STRIP.x + i * cw;
      ctx.fillStyle = side[i] ? WARM : ACC;
      ctx.globalAlpha = side[i] ? 0.55 : 0.85;
      ctx.fillRect(x, STRIP.y, Math.max(1, cw - (cw > 4 ? 1.5 : 0)), STRIP.h);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      if (i === lastMoved && lastMovedAge < 1) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},${0.9 * (1 - lastMovedAge)})`;
        ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.strokeRect(x - 1, STRIP.y - 2, Math.max(1, cw - (cw > 4 ? 1.5 : 0)) + 2, STRIP.h + 4);
      }
    }
    label(
      `${fromLn(lnOmega[nLeft])} different strips give this same count, that count is all an observer sees`,
      STRIP.x,
      STRIP.y + STRIP.h + 17,
      0.4
    );
  }

  function drawChart() {
    const N = state.N;
    const lnMax = lnOmega[N >> 1];
    const bw = CH.w / (N + 1);

    // bars: entropy S(n) = ln Ω(n)
    for (let n = 0; n <= N; n++) {
      const h = (lnOmega[n] / (lnMax || 1)) * CH.h;
      const x = CH.x + n * bw;
      ctx.fillStyle = n === nLeft ? `rgba(${ink()},0.85)` : `rgba(${ink()},0.16)`;
      ctx.fillRect(x + 0.5, CH.y + CH.h - h, Math.max(1, bw - 1), h);
    }

    // line: probability P(n) = Ω(n)/2^N, scaled to the panel
    const lnTot = N * Math.LN2;
    const pMax = Math.exp(lnMax - lnTot);
    ctx.strokeStyle = WARM;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    for (let n = 0; n <= N; n++) {
      const p = Math.exp(lnOmega[n] - lnTot) / pMax;
      const x = CH.x + (n + 0.5) * bw;
      const y = CH.y + CH.h - p * CH.h;
      n ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    // dots: measured share of time in each macrostate, same scaling
    if (state.hist && steps > 0) {
      let tot = 0;
      for (let n = 0; n <= N; n++) tot += visits[n];
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      for (let n = 0; n <= N; n++) {
        if (!visits[n]) continue;
        const f = visits[n] / tot / pMax;
        const x = CH.x + (n + 0.5) * bw;
        const y = CH.y + CH.h - Math.min(1.15, f) * CH.h;
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(x, y, 2.2, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fill();
      }
    }

    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.25)`;
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(CH.x, CH.y + CH.h);
    ctx.lineTo(CH.x + CH.w, CH.y + CH.h);
    ctx.stroke();

    // "you are here" pointer over the current macrostate
    const hx = CH.x + (nLeft + 0.5) * bw;
    const hy = CH.y + CH.h - (lnOmega[nLeft] / (lnMax || 1)) * CH.h;
    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.85)`;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(hx, hy - 6);
    ctx.lineTo(hx - 5, hy - 14);
    ctx.lineTo(hx + 5, hy - 14);
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
    label(`now: n = ${nLeft}`, hx, hy - 19, 0.75, 'center', 11);

    label('bars: entropy S(n) = ln Ω(n)', CH.x, CH.y - 14, 0.5);
    ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
    ctx.font = '12px ui-monospace, monospace';
    ctx.fillText('line: probability Ω(n)/2^N', CH.x + 220, CH.y - 14);
    if (state.hist) {
      ctx.fillStyle = ACC;
      ctx.fillText('dots: fraction of time actually spent there', CH.x + 440, CH.y - 14);
    }
    label('n = 0', CH.x, CH.y + CH.h + 16, 0.45);
    label(`n = ${N}`, CH.x + CH.w, CH.y + CH.h + 16, 0.45, 'right');
    label('all right', CH.x, CH.y + CH.h + 30, 0.3);
    label('all left', CH.x + CH.w, CH.y + CH.h + 30, 0.3, 'right');
  }

  function drawTrace() {
    const sMax = state.N * Math.LN2;
    ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(${ink()},0.22)`;
    ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(TR.x, TR.y);
    ctx.lineTo(TR.x + TR.w, TR.y);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    if (trace.length > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = ACC;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let i = 0; i < trace.length; i++) {
        const x = TR.x + (TR.w * i) / (trace.length - 1);
        const y = TR.y + TR.h - (trace[i] / (sMax || 1)) * TR.h;
        i ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y);
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    label('S / k over time', TR.x, TR.y - 12, 0.5);
    label(`S_max = N ln 2 = ${sMax.toFixed(1)}`, TR.x + TR.w, TR.y - 4, 0.4, 'right');
    label('0', TR.x - 8, TR.y + TR.h, 0.4, 'right');
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    drawBox();
    drawStrip();
    drawChart();
    drawTrace();
  }

  // --- microstate sampler (panel inset) ------------------------------------
  const micro = document.getElementById('micro') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const microSetup = setupCanvas(micro, () => drawMicro());
  let microSamples: Uint8Array[] = [];
  let microFor = -1;
  let lastMicro = 0;

  /** A uniform random microstate with exactly `n` particles on the left. */
  function sampleMicrostate(n: number) {
    const N = state.N;
    const arr = new Uint8Array(N);
    let left = n;
    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
      // pick each slot with the exact conditional probability
      if (Math.random() < left / (N - i)) {
        arr[i] = 1;
        left--;
      }
    }
    return arr;
  }
  function refreshMicro(force = false) {
    const now = performance.now();
    // Redraw only when the macrostate changed, and at most a few times a second.
    if (!force && (nLeft === microFor || now - lastMicro < 400)) return;
    lastMicro = now;
    microFor = nLeft;
    microSamples = [];
    for (let k = 0; k < 8; k++) microSamples.push(sampleMicrostate(nLeft));
    drawMicro();
  }
  function drawMicro() {
    const c = microSetup.ctx, w = microSetup.W, h = microSetup.H;
    c.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);
    const N = state.N;
    const pad = 8;
    const cw = (w - 2 * pad) / N;
    const rowH = (h - 2 * pad) / 8;
    for (let k = 0; k < microSamples.length; k++) {
      const row = microSamples[k];
      const y = pad + k * rowH;
      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        const x = pad + i * cw;
        c.fillStyle = row[i] ? ACC : WARM;
        c.globalAlpha = row[i] ? 0.85 : 0.35;
        c.fillRect(x, y, Math.max(1, cw - (cw > 4 ? 1 : 0)), rowH - 2);
      }
    }
    c.globalAlpha = 1;
  }

  // --- readouts ------------------------------------------------------------
  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  /** A duration given by its log10 in seconds, in whatever unit reads best. */
  function humanTime(log10s: number) {
    if (log10s < 7.5) {
      const s = Math.pow(10, log10s);
      if (s < 90) return `${s.toPrecision(2)} s`;
      if (s < 5400) return `${(s / 60).toPrecision(2)} min`;
      if (s < 172800) return `${(s / 3600).toPrecision(2)} hours`;
      return `${(s / 86400).toPrecision(2)} days`;
    }
    const log10y = log10s - Math.log10(3.15576e7);
    if (log10y < 7) {
      const y = Math.round(Math.pow(10, log10y));
      return `${y.toLocaleString()} year${y === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
    }
    const ratio = log10y - Math.log10(1.38e10);
    return ratio < 1
      ? `10^${Math.round(log10y)} years`
      : `10^${Math.round(log10y)} yr, 10^${Math.round(ratio)} × age of universe`;
  }
  const setEq = equationBar();
  function updateReadout() {
    const N = state.N;
    const lnO = lnOmega[nLeft];
    el('nl').textContent = `${nLeft} left, ${N - nLeft} right`;
    el('omega').textContent = fromLn(lnO);
    el('ent-s').textContent = lnO.toFixed(3);
    el('smax').textContent = (N * Math.LN2).toFixed(3);
    const share = Math.exp(lnO - N * Math.LN2);
    el('share').textContent =
      share > 0.001 ? `${(share * 100).toFixed(2)}%` : `10^${Math.round(Math.log10(share))}`;
    el('steps').textContent = steps.toLocaleString();
    // Mean return time to a state of probability p is 1/p steps, so 2^N here.
    el('recur').textContent = `${fromLn(N * Math.LN2)} steps`;
    el('recur-t').textContent = humanTime(N * Math.log10(2) - Math.log10(stepsPerSecond(state.speed)));
    el('microcap').textContent = `8 of the ${fromLn(lnO)} arrangements that look identical from outside`;
    setEq([
      [
        ['S/k = \\ln\\Omega', ACC],
        '\\quad\\text{and }\\Omega\\text{ is largest when the two halves are level}',
      ],
      [
        `\\Omega = ${texBig(lnO)}`,
        [`\\quad S/k = ${lnO.toFixed(3)}`, ACC],
        `\\quad\\max = N\\ln 2 = ${(N * Math.LN2).toFixed(3)}`,
        `\\quad\\text{share }${share > 0.001 ? (share * 100).toFixed(2) + '\\%' : '10^{' + Math.round(Math.log10(share)) + '}'}`,
      ],
      [
        'nothing pushes the gas to spread: there are simply far more ways to be spread than to be bunched',
      ],
    ]);
  }

  // --- loop ----------------------------------------------------------------
  let last = performance.now();
  let carry = 0; // fractional steps owed, so speeds below 1/frame still work
  function frame(now: number) {
    const dt = Math.min(0.05, (now - last) / 1000);
    last = now;
    if (state.running) {
      carry += dt * stepsPerSecond(state.speed);
      const n = Math.min(6000, Math.floor(carry));
      carry -= n;
      for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) stepOnce();
      trace.push(lnOmega[nLeft]);
      if (trace.length > 420) trace.shift();
    }
    for (let i = 0; i < state.N; i++) if (anim[i] < 1) anim[i] = Math.min(1, anim[i] + dt * 4);
    lastMovedAge = Math.min(99, lastMovedAge + dt * 1.4);
    draw();
    refreshMicro();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls ------------------------------------------------------------
  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('step').addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = false;
    runBtn.textContent = 'Run';
    stepOnce();
    trace.push(lnOmega[nLeft]);
    if (trace.length > 420) trace.shift();
    draw();
    refreshMicro(true);
    updateReadout();
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', () => {
    reset();
    refreshMicro(true);
  });

  const nEl = el('n') as HTMLInputElement;
  nEl.addEventListener('input', () => {
    state.N = +nEl.value;
    el('nval').textContent = nEl.value;
    build();
    refreshMicro(true);
  });
  const spEl = el('sp') as HTMLInputElement;
  const showSpeed = () => {
    const sps = stepsPerSecond(state.speed);
    el('spval').textContent =
      sps >= 10 ? `${Math.round(sps)}/s` : sps >= 1 ? `${sps.toFixed(1)}/s` : `1 step / ${(1 / sps).toFixed(1)} s`;
  };
  spEl.addEventListener('input', () => {
    state.speed = +spEl.value;
    showSpeed();
  });
  const histEl = el('hist') as HTMLInputElement;
  histEl.addEventListener('change', () => (state.hist = histEl.checked));

  build();
  showSpeed();
  refreshMicro(true);
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

